         <div type="bio">
            <p>International diplomat. He worked as a journalist at age 17, and eventually became news editor of the <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Weekly Freeman</name>. In 1923 he joined the Irish Free State Department of External Affairs and in 1929 represented Ireland to the League of Nations in Geneva. Appointed to a position in the League in 1933, he became the League’s acting Secretary General in September 1940. JJ contacted Lester in December 1940 with a request for assistance in obtaining permission to allow <name type="person" key="joyc07">Lucia</name> to leave France and to enter Switzerland. Lester retired from the League in 1946, and died in Ireland in 1959. <hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
